    "support": "full",
    "support_note": "headless-extended (deviations D-149): the undo history an interactive Blender keeps, from the session start or the last file load (blender -b keeps none until ed.undo_push()); every operator with the UNDO option, every RNA assignment and every RNA function call that changed data pushes a step (in Edit Mode only those on the edit data), ed.undo_push() pushes a named one; edit.undo_steps (32) steps are kept",
    "headless": "extended",
    "planned": "M8",
    "extension": false,
    "notes": [
      "the response's changes name the datablocks that came back (added), went away (removed) or changed (modified); result.undone names the step undone",
      "in Edit Mode an Edit Mesh / Edit Armature step restores the edit data only (as Blender's edit-mode undo types)"
    ]
  }
